<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n74434" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὀπηδ-έω</span></b> , 
			Dor.
		
		<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὀπᾱδέω</span></b>  (v. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὀπηδός</span>), used by <i><span class="en">
			Hom.
		</span></i> only in 3sg.
		pres.
		<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὀπηδεῖ,</span> and impf.
		<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὀπήδει</span> (without augm.): inf.
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b>
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὀπηδεῖν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>h.Ap.</u>
					530
				</span></i>
			 :—<i>follow, accompany, attend,</i>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τινι</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				Il.
				2.184
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				24.368
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Pi.
				<u>P.</u>
				4.287
			</span></i> ; also 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἅμα τινί</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Od.
					7.165
				</span></i>
			, <i><span class="en">
				Hes.
				<u>Th.</u>
				80
			</span></i>, <u>h.Ap.</u> l. c. ; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μετά
				τινι,</span>
			v. infr. <i><span class="en">
				11
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> of things
			(cf. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἕπομαι</span> II), <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀνεμώλια γάρ μοι ὀπηδεῖ [τόξα]</span>
			useless do they <i>go with</i> me, <i><span class="en">
				Il.
				5.216
			</span></i> ; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀρετὴν σὴν . . , ἥ τοι ὀπηδεῖ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Od.
					8.237
				</span></i>
			 ; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐκ δὲ Διὸς τιμὴ καὶ κῦδος ὀπηδεῖ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					17.251
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Hes.
				<u>Op.</u>
				142
			</span></i>,<i><span class="en">
				313
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Thgn.
				933
			</span></i>, etc. ; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μετ᾽ ἀνδράσι λιμὸς ὀπηδεῖ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hes.
					<u>Op.</u>
					230
				</span></i>
			 ; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μετ᾽ ἴχνια Κύρνος ὀ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Call.
					<u>Del.</u>
					19
				</span></i>
			.—
				Ep.
			 Verb, rare in Trag., as 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὀπαδεῖ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.
					<u>Fr.</u>
					475
				</span></i>
			 ; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὀπαδοῦσ᾽</span> prob. in <i><span class="en">
				Id.
				<u>Ag.</u>
				426
			</span></i> (lyr.), and once in a late Pap., <i><span class="en">
				<u>Sammelb.</u>
				4324.11
			</span></i> (Tab. Defix.) : <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὀπαδός</span>
			however is used by Trag.</div>
